New in 7.0.0 (2026-11-13):
- module -T: made the cylinder and sphere domains exact (curved, also
  for a cylinder periodic along z), added -domain hourglass, improved
  cutting algorithm (now direct cutting), fixed -transform planecut and
  other cut operations, added -morphooptilogdis curpdf0 and -transform
  rmtess,
  improved -morpho (void cells), fixed -ori, fixed -stattesr vol, added
  periodic multiscale tessellations, improved regularization (3D),
  removed [r]sel from -morpho, enabled expressions in all -stat options,
  fixed build-dependent regularization results and a buffer overflow for
  periodic tessellations, fixed face equations after regularization, set
  face equations on curved domain faces to tangent planes, labeled the
  curved domain face cyl or hourglass, added -transform renamedomface,
  fixed non-deterministic -morpho optimization (thread race in the
  evaluation of distributions), sped up the computation of the cells
  (about 25% faster -morpho), sped up the neighbor search during -morpho
  (rebuilt kd-tree), fixed memory leaks, a double free with -morpho
  lamellar and buffer overflows with -domain stdtriangle and
  -morphooptistop, fixed Ctrl+C after a -morpho optimization (it was
  ignored, e.g. during regularization), added -regdelcell (deletion of
  cells during regularization), renamed -regularization, -fmax, -[r]sel,
  -mloop and -maxedgedelqty to -reg, -regfmax, -reg[r]sel, -regloop and
  -regedgedelmax (the former names are deprecated), fixed 2D
  regularization (crash), made minor fixes, named the input file of
  -format sim after the output file (e.g. n5-id1.tess, instead of
  simulation.tess), added -transform rmseed and the seed keys
  cell_<key> (keys of the seed's cell), fixed partial periodicity
  (e.g. -periodicity x) and face orientations (now all outwards) of
  periodic single-cell and -morpho cube tessellations, fixed
  regularization of curved domains (a domain face, e.g. the end of a
  cylinder, could lose all its faces), fixed the orientation of the
  faces on curved domain faces (now all outwards; they could point
  inwards, e.g. with -transform cut), added val<1e-12 to the
  -morphooptistop default value, kept the cylinder and sphere domains
  exact when translated or rotated, removed the transformations of
  -loadtesr (use -transform), fixed -transform translate and rotate on
  curved domains (stale domain face parameters and face points),
  enabled -transform rmseed and cut(...,algo=legacy) with -loadtess
  (the domain is recovered from the tessellation), made them account
  for previous transformations such as scale, fixed the geometric
  anisotropy factor of 2D tessellation faces of arbitrary orientation
  (including slices) and improved the handling of degenerate faces,
  made seed weights actual Laguerre weights (instead of their square
  roots) everywhere (see incompatible changes below), fixed the rw key
  of -orioptilogvar (it logged the Laguerre weight), fixed -ori odf
  with -orisampling uniform (crash), added a warning when -orisampling
  uniform has no effect, fixed -orisampling uniform with orientations
  loaded from a file (crash), made -orioptiini use the syntax of
  -morphooptiini (see incompatible changes below), fixed the -morpho
  distributions (CDF) with penalized cells, added an error for an
  unknown -format (it was ignored, and nothing was written), fixed
  -format svg(...) followed by other formats (error), sped up -morpho
  when a seed has an outlier weight (e.g. a seed moved out of the
  domain; the computation of all cells was slowed down, up to about
  20x), sped up the periodic full computation of the -morpho
  distributions (about 25x).
- module -M: fixed $Fasets and 2D mesh for -elt hex, added a warning for
  small elements due to a non-regularized tessellation, enabled
  expressions in all -stat options, added custom node sets to -nset
  (<label>:<expr>, min, max and closest), fixed -nset (non-default
  values were ignored), enabled -interface discontinuous and cohesive
  for periodic tessellations, fixed the labels of the cohesive element
  sets (now the interface ids), fixed the interface scales of 2D and
  periodic multiscale tessellations (-interface), fixed -interface for
  multiscale tessellations with continuous scales (the mesh was torn
  along continuous interfaces) and cohesive elements at the
  discontinuous scales, made the Gmsh library mandatory (version 4.9 or
  higher; the gmsh program is no longer used; -gmsh and -tmp are
  obsolete), set the element sizes inside the faces and cells by a mesh
  size map (increase from their boundaries at a rate set by -pl, up to
  -[r]cl; 3D sizes calibrated to the map, within -mesh3dclreps; 3D
  meshing algorithm netg no longer available), made the edge meshing
  follow the same mesh size map (equidistribution, element number
  rounded to the nearest; it was rounded up), changed the increase rate
  of the mesh size map to ln (pl) (adjacent elements of length ratio
  pl), calibrated the 2D sizes to the mesh size map too (added
  -mesh2dclreps), made the 2D multimeshing size quality account for the
  mesh size map, fixed the 3D element lengths (all edges; -statelt
  length and lengths), fixed -statelt lengths in 2D, added -[r]clpoly and -pl{edge,face,poly},
  fixed default in -[r]cl{poly,face,edge,ver} expressions (crash, and
  wrong values with -rcl*), fixed -format inp for several mesh
  dimensions (-dim): added the 0D elements, made the element numbering
  contiguous (as in msh), fixed the surface element numbers, the node
  order of 3-node line elements and the types of 1D and 2D elements of a
  3D mesh, fixed memory leaks and a buffer overflow with -elt hex,
  changed the node order of the $Fasets elements to the Gmsh order (it
  was reversed; msh version bumped to 2.4, version 2.3 still read),
  fixed the $Fasets elements of -elt hex -order 2 (they were of order
  1), removed the renumbering of nodes and elements by partition after
  partitioning (-part; left to FEPX), named the input files of -format
  sim after the output file (e.g. n5-id1.msh, instead of
  simulation.msh), fixed -loadmesh -part on a periodic mesh (crash),
  kept the node sets of a mesh loaded without the tessellation
  (-loadmesh; they were recreated from the mesh, with f* labels or, for
  a periodic mesh, from the cell boundaries), with the missing edge and
  vertex node sets obtained by intersection, and also updated with
  -order and -sortnode, removed the node sets and fasets of the periodic
  domain faces, edges and vertices (which were empty), fixed the node
  set number of $NSets when a node set is not found, fixed -sortnode
  for the fasets and cohesive elements (their nodes were not
  renumbered), fixed the meshing of the faces of a curved cylinder
  domain spanning more than 180 degrees (abort) and the back-projection
  of the curved cylinder faces, added an error message for a face that
  winds around the cylinder axis (too few cells), fixed a crash when the
  meshing of a face failed, improved the meshing of the faces of a
  curved sphere domain (conformal, stereographic projection, instead of
  a gnomonic projection, which distorted large faces) and of the torus
  faces (hourglass domain and torus cuts, conformal unrolling, instead of
  a plane projection), fixed the Gmsh worker processes, which kept
  running when neper ended during meshing (e.g. on an error), made the
  element characteristic lengths of the faces increase from those of
  their boundary nodes at the rate set by -pl (or -plface), up to the
  face value, with the length scale factor of the curved face
  projections taken into account (they were extended from the boundary
  by Gmsh), which provides elements closer to the target size, fixed
  the 1D meshing of the edges (position where the cl progressions from
  the edge extremities meet, which could lead to a progression factor
  lower than the requested one), projected the order-2 nodes of the
  curved faces and edges onto the curved domain, removed the
  transformations of the tesr input (use neper -T -transform), removed
  partitioning based on a computer architecture (-part now takes only a
  number of partitions, not necessarily a power of 2) and -partmethod
  (libscotch is always used), fixed -elt hex on a regularized
  tessellation in parallel (thread race: elements could be assigned to
  the wrong cells and results were not reproducible), added $Topology
  to the msh file of a discontinuous mesh (-interface), fixed -part with
  a Scotch library built with 64-bit integers (compilation error and
  buffer overflow), renamed -elttype hex, quad and quad9 (grid meshes)
  to hexgrid, quadgrid and quad9grid (quad9 is deprecated), and made
  -elttype hex and quad provide conformal meshes (by splitting the
  tetrahedral and triangular elements, as Gmsh does, and, in 2D,
  recombining them into quadrangular elements first), added the
  hexahedral element facets to -format inp (surfaces), restricted
  -elttype to its documented values, fixed -order 2 for 2D raster
  tessellations (crash), removed -format msh4, made unknown -format
  values fail (they were ignored, or crashed).
- module -V: added highlighting colors hl1, hl2 and hl3, fixed the
  *_shown variables of the -show* options (which depended on the option
  order), fixed memory leaks and a double free with -showvox, fixed
  -showmesh 1 also showing the tessellation, removed -colormode (dark
